        body: "A Soyuz-2.1a rocket lifted off from the Baikonur Cosmodrome on Tuesday, July 14, 2026, carrying NASA astronaut Anil Menon alongside Russian cosmonauts Pyotr Dubrov — serving as mission commander — and Anna Kikina on a two-day transit to the International Space Station, where the trio will join the existing Expedition 74 crew and restore the station to its full complement following a short-handed operating period. Menon, a physician-astronaut and SpaceX Dragon crew alumnus from the 2017 NASA class, is flying his second long-duration spaceflight as mission specialist, with his Soyuz assignment continuing the decade-long crew exchange agreement between NASA and Roscosmos that has preserved continuous human presence aboard the station through periods of vehicle development and geopolitical complexity. The Soyuz MS-29 crew is scheduled to dock at the Rassvet Mini-Research Module 1 port, joining an Expedition 74 science programme already mid-cycle on cartilage tissue engineering, cardiac health monitoring, and neurocognitive performance studies as the station prepares for the July 26 undocking of Soyuz MS-28 and the subsequent Expedition 75 handover ceremony.",
