        headline: "Expedition 74 Crew Aboard International Space Station Completes Soyuz Seat Inspections, Cargo Transfers, and CubeSat Hardware Maintenance as Station Operations Continue Nominally Through Busy July Manifest — Crew Health Checks Priority Research Objective as ISS Approaches 26 Years of Continuous Human Habitation Milestone in October 2026",
        body: "The Expedition 74 crew aboard the International Space Station conducted a productive research and maintenance day on July 10, prioritising health checks and CubeSat hardware maintenance among the research objectives while also stowing spacewalking gear, transferring cargo between visiting vehicles, and checking crew seats inside a docked Soyuz spacecraft in preparation for an upcoming crew rotation. Station operations in July 2026 are proceeding against a busy manifest that includes ongoing life sciences experiments in microgravity cellular biology, material science investigations in the Columbus and Kibo laboratory modules, and remote sensing coordination with international ground teams. CubeSat hardware maintenance — one of the priority tasks logged for this week — reflects the station's increasing role as a deployment platform for small satellites, with the NanoRacks and Japan Aerospace Exploration Agency deployment mechanisms having collectively released hundreds of small spacecraft since the capability was first established in 2012. The ISS is approaching the October 2026 milestone of 26 years of uninterrupted human habitation — a record that began with the arrival of the first Expedition 1 crew in November 2000 — as NASA and its international partners continue planning for the station's orderly deorbiting no earlier than 2030 and the transition of low Earth orbit operations to commercially operated stations.",
        sourceUrl: "https://www.nasa.gov/blogs/",
