        body: "The European Space Agency entered a new governance chapter on July 1, 2026 as Juan Carlos Cortés Pulido, Head of the Spanish Delegation, formally assumed the ESA Council Chair for a two-year term alongside Vice-Chairs Tanja Permozer of Slovenia and Kimmo Kanto of Finland — a leadership transition flowing from decisions taken at the 347th ESA Council meeting held June 16-17 at ESA Headquarters in Paris, which was chaired for the final time by outgoing Chair Renato Krpoun. The June Council meeting produced significant programmatic decisions, including authorisation for the agency to enter negotiations with potential partners and providers for the EPIC (ESA Provided Institutional Crew) professional astronaut mission concept, representing a potential step toward European crewed spaceflight capability independent of American and Russian launch arrangements. Member States approved an extension and amendment of the Cooperative Agreement between ESA and ISRO until January 2032, broadening the scope of collaboration to include human and robotic exploration, space weather research, and orbital sustainability activities — deepening European-Indian space partnership as both agencies expand their exploration ambitions. The Council also confirmed that an Interim Council at Ministerial level will convene in December 2026 in Italy to define the European exploration roadmap for the coming decade, providing a critical policy forum for aligning member states ahead of major decisions on lunar architecture and future launch vehicle competitiveness.",
